theory:
## The Silent Killer

```xiom
fn add_one(x: Int) -> Int {
  return x + 1;  // What if x is Int.MAX?
}
```

In debug mode, XIOM checks for overflow and traps. In release, it wraps silently (like C).

### Better: Checked Operations
```xiom
fn safe_add(a: Int, b: Int) -> Option[Int] {
  return a.checked_add(b);
}

fn main() -> Int {
  let x = Int.MAX;
  match safe_add(x, 1) {
    Some(v) => return v,
    None => return 0,  // Overflow handled
  }
}
```

### Checked Operations
| Operation | Safe Alternative |
|-----------|-----------------|
| a + b | a.checked_add(b) |
| a - b | a.checked_sub(b) |
| a * b | a.checked_mul(b) |
| a / b | requires: b != 0 |
| -a | a.checked_neg() |

### Saturation Pattern
```xiom
fn clamp_add(a: Int, b: Int) -> Int {
  match a.checked_add(b) {
    Some(v) => return v,
    None => if b > 0 { return Int.MAX; } else { return Int.MIN; },
  }
}
```

